WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.812
Now apply the same reasoning to e-commerce data.

00:00:02.812 --> 00:00:09.037
Device type is nominal. Membership tier is ordinal when the business defines a real rank.

00:00:09.037 --> 00:00:11.712
Session duration is a ratio measurement.

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:15.537
Purchases are a ratio count.

00:00:15.537 --> 00:00:21.942
Weekday is interesting because it is often treated as a nominal or cyclical category rather than a simple

00:00:21.942 --> 00:00:22.272
ordinal variable.

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:30.047
Revenue is a ratio-scale monetary amount, but its database storage should use exact arithmetic and document

00:00:30.047 --> 00:00:36.412
currency. Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:41.877
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:49.252
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:49.252 --> 00:00:54.927
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:54.927 --> 00:01:00.733
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
